FriendsFest: Comedy Series That Teacher Teased Important Lessons About Friendship Between Men
Absence of similar characters in the series is obvious, given that the need for men to open is now more desperate than ever, suicide rates among young men reaching the peak of the last 15 years.
In 2013, Suicide was the leading cause of death in 20-45-year-a-year-aged men in the UK, and remains three times more common in men than in women.
In an attempt to address the problem, the Campaign Against Living Miserably (CALM) designated 2015 as the Year of the Man, wanting to call into question the culture that prevents men from asking for help when they need it.
Friendship is at the center of the fight towards the success of this challenge.
A recent study of more than 2000 high school pupils who showed symptoms of depressed have concluded that if the patient is surrounded by enough “healthy-stained friends”, his chances of recovery double.
Equally, for people who aren't depressed, a circle of mentally healthy friends halves the likelihood of mental disorders.
Of course, in order for the friendship to have an effect, it must in the first and foremost be accessible.
In this era of social media-dominitated communication, where the emphasis is placed on style and not on the substance, the Immediate character of the answer often takes precedence over meaningful contact.
“Digital lives have doubled the need to create the sepulation of a strong personality, open to fun and success, even if it’s in reality it’s confinishing that dominates.
This superficial success is dominated by what psychiatrists call extrinsic values; the money, the image, social status, all at the cost of intrinsic values - our inner desire for personal development and friendship - that even more profoundly affect our mental health.
Inventurer Billiary of a Video Game Recently Explained That Money Really Doesn't Buy Happiness.
The beauty of the series Friends was that it turned your attention to this idea.
The characters weren't defined by the workplace but by their own personality, which they showed by interacting as friends.
Humility of Joey and Chandler's frequent hugs, the moments when they look at football in comfortable chairs and Ross's passion for Rachel came from the fact that it's known that men can associate with this situation, even though they often shy away from completely exploring their feelings.
“My role to listen to people with suicidal and depressed tendencies has shown how even the smallest interactions with friends can make a difference.”
People who turn to us often don't feel able to talk to our friends.
The old advocation to fend for yourself is strong, just like the feeling of being perceived as a weak person if you talk openly about the problems.
Friends is one of the series that comes to mind when I try to provide more long-haired psychological coping mechanisms.
The series highlighted the small moments of friendship between men.
No matter how much objective, out-of-the-above intervention helps via the phone, people who arrive in moments of deprivation, long-term support comes from family and close-failed friends.
Thus, if you participate this weekend at the FriendsFest organized by Comedy Central, with the complete rendering of the sets to Celebrate the Event, why do not invite your friends for a coffee in Central Perk.
Or, even better yet, if you see someone alone in Starbucks, smile and say hello.
There’s never any difference your friendship.
