Quarrh Career Fair offers thousands of jobs in 200 firms
200 companies are awaited at the Autumn Quaranto Quiet (TdC), an event that will take place in Brasov, Chisinau, Cluj-Napoca, Iasi, Sibiu and Tirgu-Mures.
The companies have vacancies several thousand jobs, internship opportunities and trainee internships, and some of them are already announced on the official website www.targuldecariere.ro.
Recruiting an ever-greasing Prioritary Priority for Companies
According to the statistics made following the 100 editions so far of the Quarrel Fair, most of the companies are interested, in addition to the effective recruitment, to develop a strong employer brand among young people: 97% of their representatives said they want to go back to the next editions, while 94% said they recommend TdC as a recruitment and employer branding solution.
There are also cases in which the companies choose to pack their jobs, precisely because in this way they can think more organized recruits.
Among those who will check the attendance list at TdC in October and November 2015 included: Arvato Bertelsmann, Bombardier, Bosch, CIE Matricon, Competence Call Center, DB Schenker, Delphi, Office Depot, Preh, Renault, Schweffler, Stefanini and Sykes.
TdC Candidate Profile
The most TdC participants who are looking for a job are students, over 59.70%, followed by university graduates - 23.05% and master's graduates: 10.38%.
The fewest are those who have completed the PhD - 0.67 - and the young people who have completed high school or middle school - 6.20%.
Regarding the areas in which they are specialized, most of them work in IT and Software, in the financial-Banking sector or in insurance, marketing, advertising and media or in the automotive and construction industries.
It’s no longer a novelty that the IT area is in a continuous ascension in the country.
As a result, there will also take place this year a new edition of the IT Career Fair, a niche event dedicated exclusively dedicated to enthusiasts and specialists in this field.
Among the giants from the business environment present at the 7th edition of the event were Accenture, Endava, KFC, McDonald's, msg systems, Siemens, Steelcase, Unicredit Business Integrated Solutions and Yardi Systems.
Cariere's Targul, 100 editions
Founded in Cluj in 2006, the Career Fair is today the largest network of career events in Romania and the Republic of Moldova.
The Autumn edition will take place in Chisinau (Martyrman’s House, 2-3 October), Iasi (Palasi, October 6-7), Brasov (Waiting House, 14-15 October), Cluj Global (Polyvalence Hall, 20-21 October), Cluj IT (Polyvalence Hall, 22-23 October), Sibiu (Business Center, 28-29 October) and Targu-Mures (National Theatre, 5 November).
Details about the companies registered so far and about the Career Fair can be found on www.targuldecariere.ro.
