How Satisfied Are Romans in a Couple: Men versus Women
Most of the Romanians are satisfied with their relationships.
This is the conclusion of a study carried out on the occasion of John Gray’s coming to Romania, the famous author of “Men are from Mars, Women are from Venus”.
A total of 62% of responders declare themselves 'very satisfied' and "satisfied" by the overall quality of the couple's relationship.
"However, 18% appear to be 'easily unsatisfied' and 'relautifully unsatisfied' in the relationship, and another 18 per cent said 'fulfill,'" the study said in a press release.
The situation is slightly different when the responses of men and women are analysed separately.
Thus, 28% of the men are very satisfied, 39% satisfied, 17% suitable, 6% 6% unsatisfied and 8% slightly unsatisfied.
Regarding women, 33% were satisfied, 24% very satisfied, 8% very unsatisfied, 14% slightly unsatisfied and 19% chose the right category.
When we look at satisfaction (positive), we'll notice that men are more satisfied.
Regarding the neutra state (appropriately), we see a difference of two percent.
"Since the very unsatisfactory situation, the biggest difference being the slightly unsatisfactory answer where we see a difference of 6 percent," the statement reads.
The study also showed that a quarter of Romanians (26 per cent) spend an hour or even less time together, 18 per cent spend between five and eight hours together, and 45 per cent between two and four hours.
The authors of the study also say that "Romanians feel a little more adventure in their lives (24%), followed by affection (21%), money (21%), safety (20%), new (19 per cent, sex (19 per cent, respect 17%, 17% confidence, 17% pleasure, 17% connection, knowledge 16%, protection 14%, importance 14%, learning 12 per cent, 11 per cent self-knowledge and 7% control."
The study was conducted by Extreme Training between June 1 and September 1 on 1,369 people, the error margin calculated being 2.6 per cent.
