And it was good to plummet before its main opponent was the Islamic State.
For a couple of years there has been a featus between the Assad regime and moderate militias, bolstered by Gulf and Western countries.
Then the Islamic State arrived and now we don't know if we want the Assad regime to fall.
Russia was able to accomplice things, but it can't take part in the solution.
It creates outbreaks of instability and chaos it can't shut down.
