Which button will appear soon
Millions of Facebook users have become accustomed to "Like" button, and now the representatives of the social network are forge the other opposite, that of "Dislike".
On Tuesday, Mark Zuckerberg, co-founder and chief executive of the company, announced on his account that this button will be available soon, the New York Times reported on the blog.
Zuckerberg made it clear that "Dislike" button will rather show a nuance of what a user feels than a simple option.
However, its ad raised the question that Facebook could become a less-than-voiced place.
“Kitukovoker says he wants to avoid moments when someone is posting an important event in life, and someone else will “Dislike.”
The users of the network, which has reached 1.5 billion active accounts, have for a long time demanded the opportunity to express negative emotions or empathy with something sad.
Mark Zuckerberg also said it was uncoiled for people “Like” to current events, such as the refugee crisis, or in the event of a death of a family member.
"You may not feel comfortable to like that post," the Facebook representative pointed out.
The variant of a new button on Facebook has not been well received by everyone.
"There's already enough hate on Facebook and on social media," Atiq Haneef in Afghanistan commented on the New York Times Facebook page, where the article was tapped.
"I'll 'Dislike' the 'Dislike' button," he said.
Roger Anderson, a microbiologist in Atlanta, claimed there is nothing wrong with this button, emphasizing people to have different opinions on Facebook.
Debra Aho Williamson, a social media outstand at eMarketer, mentioned that it’s hard to conceiter that a single-button can convey a complex range of negative emotions.
What's more, she argues, the election campaign is approaching in America, and the "Dislike" button would create an all-terresting disaster.
Only 70 refugees entered Hungary within 24 hours
LONG (Reuters) - Hungary on Tuesday accepted only 70 migrants, one-bove thousands of mass-comers at its border with Serbia, government adviser Gyorgy Bakondi said.
Hungary declared a state of emergency during the day in two counties along the border with Serbia due to the flow of refugees, shutting down a main border crossing point and announcing that it will build a fence on its border with Romania.
The measure drew a sudden reaction from Serbia.
Just yesterday they said they would tilt the border for those who want to cross, but not for those who want to ask for asylum.
"As you can see, this is totally different," Serbian Refugee Minister Aleksandar Vulin said.
BEHwd, a record 5,809 migrants entered Hungary on Sunday, the police said.
More than 170,000 migrants from the Middle East and Africa also broke into Hungary from Serbia in 2015.
“Mriers avoid being registered and trying to reach the West, especially in Germany.
"Northern" County Council headquarters is about to fail.
Two Builders in Insolvencies
The massive investments made here in recent years, with a view to relieving the institution, stand to collapse because they have been halted several times.
Two important builders who worked here went into insolvencies during the works.
The headquarters of the County Council in Vasile Alecsandri Street will end up crumbling on its own.
At a year and a half since the consolidation and refunctionalization of the building should have been completed, the works have not even reached the half.
A final stage in the epic of the building was consumed the other day, when the National Council for Settlement of Complaints (CNSC) rejected a complaint of the company that wanted to take over the contract for the realization of the technical project for the works still to be executed.
The initial project was compiled by Impex Romcatel SA.
After the insolvency of the builder and the interruption of the works, the negotiation procedures were started without the publication of a participation notice with Impex Romcatel, the company will update the technical project, and then a new tender for the works will be organized.
"Negotiations have not been finalized through a contract, the CJ appreciating that the proposed form would have disadvantaged the institution," Razvan Timofciuc summarized, represented public relations within the CJ.
The CJ’s decision to interrupt the direct negotiations was challenged in court by Impex Romcatel.
The Iasi court sent the complaint to the CNSC, which dismissed it as late.
However, this does not imply that CJ can start the search for another designer.
Impex Romcatel has the possibility to appeal the CNSC’s decision at the Court of Appeal, only after a final sentence of it can be taken into account the finding of another designer.
Thus, the consolidation of the building could be resumed at the earliest next year.
Our intention is to re-start the work as soon as possible.
In principle, the restoration of the technical project shouldn't take a long time, but we have to come to the conclusion of a contract.
"Wait until we see if CNSC's decision will be challenged or not," Timofciuc said.
The consolidation works of the former Headquarters of the Police Matter began in 2011.
A first works contract was terminated in April 2012, after works were carried out of 4.5 million lei.
The auction was resumed, the contract being adjudicated by Moldoconstruct SA.
However, the company went into insolvencies, and this contract was terminated, after payments of RON 1.5 million had been made.
The works have been carried out so far at about 50 per cent.
Initially, the works of consolidating, refunctionalization and attics of the building had been valued at 7.7 million lei.
"Okay, I'm saying it all!" - the statement that could incriminate the ex-president chief of Cadastre
One of the employees involved in the outrageous dossier at the Cadastre Office has signed an agreement to acknowledge the facts, against adjournment.
Most likely, his statements will incriminate the other defendants, led by the ex-chief, Narciza Nedelcu
An Adviser from the Office of Cadastre and Real Estate Advertising (OCPI) Iasi accused by the DNA in a corruption dossier admitted his actions.
The agreement on recognisiation signed by Dumitru Dascălu was registered yesterday at the Iasi Court, the judges agreeing to give a solution in this case on September 29.
Dumitru Daniel Dascălu was accused of intellectual forgery in continuous form and he agreed to execute two-year impriminent imprisonment, as well as community service.
Regarding the facts imputed to Dascalu, the prosecutors specified that he, as an adviser to the Cadastre Office, together with other colleagues, "blatantly compilied several minutes of acceptance, regarding the service contracts previously concluded by O.C.P.I. Iași with the administrators of the companies SC Gauss SRL, SC Grup Five SRL, SC Topo Euro Cad SRL
The other day, the ex-chief of the Office, Narciza Nedelcu, as well as other former or current OCPI employees were prosecuted in this case, the accusations being the settlement of some services to the mentioned companies, although the works have not been carried out.
Prejudice exceeds 300,000 lei.
Aflaws in the Stone Age
According to FRH President Alexandru Dedu, Romania can host a major handball competition only in 2024, and the preparation of the women's national handball team to qualify the Olympium costs a fortune.
The President of the Romanian Handball Federation, Alexandru Dedu, stated yesterday, during a meeting with the press, that there is a great pride that our country has three teams in the Champions League groups.
Regarding Romania's women's women's national handball team, "the main objective is to qualify at the Rio Olympics, but for this we have to go through two stages of caudulas, in the first place the World Championship and in the 2nd row the prequalification tournament", Dedu also said.
We very much want to qualify for the Olympics.
It's some fantastic demands on the part of the technical staff led by Tomas Ryde.
Stag that will consist of seven or eight people.
"He wants the assistant coach, a doctor, two masseurs, the coach of the goalkeepers, physical preparer, delegation chief.
They asked us to obtain some things for qualification, more precisely materials for physical preparation that we have never ever heard of.
That's all to get to the Olympic Games, and I'm going to do my best to have.
We're talking a massive investment, there's a lot, there's a lot of money.
But that's the road to perform.
'Cause at the moment we're in the stone age with preparation.
"The teams we're battling with have these materials and they've had them for some time," said Dedu, who noted that he was trying to obtain the necessary amounts for the purchase of these products from MTS and COSR.
The FRH President also referred to the infrastructure in Romania and the possibility that our country will host a major handball competition.
We don't have room in Bucharest.
It's an infrastructure problem and it's disgraceful to question a European Gymnastic Gymnastics Championship.
Let's not forget that in other corners of the world Olympic neighborhoods have been built entirely within two years.
Before 1992, there was a landfill of rubbish, and now it has become a landmark of beauty.
The same was the case in London, where the organization of the 2012 Olympiad was also a success in terms of investments.
"In my vision, in 2024 we can host a major competition," Dedu said.
"He added that the international handball bodies are willing to grant Romania the organization of a major competition.
For me it is a priority to bring major handball competitions in Romania.
Mr. Gatu went civilized with a project, the people gave their consent in principle, but it was clarified very quickly that the hall will never be built.
And I had discussions with EHF, I told them that we want, that we are able to organize and they said that I agree and invite them to the first match in the new room in Bucharest and after that we discuss concretely.
"So we've got the whole open opener, and at the EHF, but we don't have any infrastructure," the FRH official explained.
The former great hand-ball player avoided evaluating the chances of CSM Bucharest and HCM Baia Mare’s women’s teams from arriving in the Final Four: “I have asked all the coaches to be reserved in prognostications, that if they don’t come back against them.”
A good road to the World Cup
Romanian rugby players start on September 23 against France
National rugby team captain Mihai Macovei told at a press conference on Tuesday that all Romania's team members are ready for the World Cup matches in England, where he hopes to achieve two victories: "We are ready".
Both I and my colleagues are with engines at full speed.
We've been coaching to deliver the best-perceusion in our four games.
Everyone will have high-expectations, because our goal is to win in two matches, against Canada and Italy.
All the groups are heavy and ours is the same.
Let's take it easy, the first time with France and then we'll see it.
