"We want you to be very proud that some players, a small family like rugby in Romania, proudly represents the tricolour," Macovei said.
Romania’s national team manager, Lynn Howells, at the first experience as a coach at the World Cup, hopes to make the Romanians proud of the rugby selection: “It’s a great honor for us to take part in this World Cup”.
I'm sure the players are ready to participate in the tournament.
It's an extraordinary experience for me.
For me it is very very important that at every match I make the Romanians proud of the national team.
The President of the Romanian Rugby federation, Haralambie Dumitraș, is confident that the Romanian players can confirm the progress made in recent years in rugby.
