At the Rugby Women's World Cup in England, Romania will perform in Group D, with the following matches scheduling the following matches: with France, on 23 September in London; with Ireland on September 27 in London; with Canada on October 6 at Leicester; with Italy on October 11 at Exeter.
The competition kick-starts on Friday at the Twickenham Stadium in London with the England - Fiji Group A match.
New Japanese Culture Courses Organized at "Al.I. Cuza University"
About Flower Arrangements in a Fowl, ink painting, but also a casual study about the beautiful arts specific to the Country of the Rising Soda you can learn in the courses organized by the students from Iasi.
The JAPAen Cultural Students’ Circle in Iasi organizes new courses of Japanese culture (ikebana, summit and beautiful arts) between October 2015 and June 2016, courses for both beginners and opinionated people.
They will take place at the "Al. I. Cuza" University Center in Iasi and are organized in order to promote the Japanese, traditional and modern arts and culture.
For these there is a single participation fee of 50 lei per month per person.
Apart from the art lessons, the attendees will be able to take part in the realization of exhibitions and other cultural activities to promote beauty.
The courses of Japanese culture that we proposed to you were conceived as an invitation, addressed to the general public, to realize the first steps on the road to self-knowledge through art.
"Interested persons will be able to find out how to make harmonious floral sculptural creations (ikebanas), how to capture the soul of the surrounding elements in plastic compositions using the Japanese art of in-cough painting (Sumie) or how to express their own individuality and creativity through the plurivalent universe of beautiful arts (graph, drawing, painting)," Sorin Mazilu, the teacher of these courses.
The courses are addressed to everyone who is passionate about art, regardless of age or experience.
Enrolments take place until September 30, and those who want to ask for more information can be done at: 0742.027.153 or at the e-mail address: studenticulture@gmail.com.
14 Million Dollars Given to "St. Spiridon" Hospital in Iasi at budget rectification
What will be purchased with this important amount of money?
"St. Spiridon" Hospital received from the Ministry of Health, following the budget rectification, about 14 million lei.
The money that the medical unit has received to use by the end of the year will be invested in the modernization and furnishing works of some clinics, but also in equipment and medical equipment for which the hospital has already started the public procurement procedure.
Thus, the sanitary unit will be equipped with a new tomography computer, a new radiology device, with six kits used for surgical interventions, six properly-equipped ITI beds, ophthalmological microscope and other appliances necessary to carry out the medical act.
On the other hand, 5 million lei from the money received by the hospital will be directed to the construction and furnishing of the "Great Ars".
From the money from the budgetary rectification, UPU will receive 500,000 lei for the completion of the modernization works in the main section.
"Furthermore, in the coming days we will do the reception of the works from the walkway linking the UPU to the cardiology, hepatology and gastroenterology clinics to ensure decent transport of the patient from UPU into neighboring clinics," the medical unit manager also explained.
The hospital will soon have in the yard the Dermatology Clinic in Tătăraşi, which it will organize in the outpatient, in the same form in which it currently operates.
The clinic will operate in the area where allergology, haematology and ambulatory endocrinology is located and will have about 30 beds.
Iasi, embarrassed by RATP controllers and a leaflet.
Pity of a tourist
A family of tourists from Cluj came to Iasi to visit him, but the excursion ended with a bitter promise.
According to the lived experience, neither I nor my wife want to step in your city again.
Unwitttingly, they bumped the erroneous information from the leaflets, the insensitivity of RAPT controllers and, bonus, a fine “that’s what the law says”.
Husbands Arrived in Iasi A Few Days A Few Days Ago, Stayed in a hotel in the Center and requested tourist leaflets.
They also received a flyer where RATP trails were written.
"Animated" with these maps, the spouses visited Iasi.
But, two days ago, in Copou, they wanted to reach the Palas Mall.
Since there was no tonnage with tickets in the station near Copou Park, they relied on the information printed on the leaflet: that they can get a ticket by SMS.
"No one's told them this service doesn't exist anymore.
Confessful in the leaflet, they got on a bus and they tried to send an e-smuggling after the instructions on the leaflet.
Unfortunantly for them, a RATP team emerged.
They said that there is no service for 2 years and that it was announced in the press that it was canceled.
WHENESOESIBODY I WOULOTE what was written in the local press, me coming the night before I visited the city?
I've talked to the controllers, I've explained the situation to them, they've said they don't care, it's none of their business.
Attitude was very defiant.
They’ve said that all they can do is give us a single fine instead of 2 (mi and my wife).
“I paid, I didn’t want to ruin my visiting day at the gendarmerie and giving statements there!” says Ovidiu.
In conclusion, the family was fined because of erroneous information on the flyer and controllers who "applied the law to the blood."
It’s not right, and I made a complaint at RATP Iasi to get my money back.
It’s not about money, it’s not a lot, it’s not a lot, but the point is that I’ve felt deluded.
Unlucky for rapists in Vaslui.
They had an injury and remained in pre-trial detainee
The trial of Vaslui’s seven rapists has moved yesterday to the Iasi Court of Appeal.
Magistrates from Iasi judged the first trial term in an unpublimatory meeting in which the seven young men accused of scoundreling an 18-year-old girl asked to be released.
Before the actual beginning of the hearing, one of the judges from Iasi to whom the case had been assigned, Viorel Munteanu, made a request for abstention, which was admitted by his colleagues from the court.
The Magistrate acted until the summer of this year at the Vaslui Court, where he was the President of the Penational Section, who, on April 9, admitted an appeal formulated by four of the defendants, ordering their placement under house arrest.
At the moment, the dossier is prosecuted by a panel of Magistries Maricica Mititelu and Geta Sandu.
Previously, a abstention in the filth and Judge Dan Anthon, on the grounds that his daughter was in a cohabitation relationship with one of the rapist’s lawyers.
The two justices have decided that Vaslui rapists will still remain in pre-trial detainee.
The young people will remain incarcerated for at least 30 more days, when the judges re-discuss the possibility of release.
The next hearing will take place at the Iasi Court of Appeal on October 6.
Before arriving at the Iasi Court of Appeal, the van with which the rapists from Vaslui were transported was involved in an accident occurred in Păcurari district, the car entering Iasi on the belt.
The Iveco van with whom the seven rapists were transported hit a Volks-wagen car that had come out of Canta Street, and the driver tried to turn to the left.
The van circulates from the end Păcurari.
The car entered Iasi here because the employees of the Penitentiary Administration preferred the route from Vaslui to Iasi at the Stables, and then on the ring road.
They darted the road by a few kilometers.
Immediately after the impact, the arrestee's escort summoned another consignment to take over the detainees.
In a short time, a car was dispatched to the site of the Iasi Maximum Security Penitentiary, which picked up the seven detainees and transported them to the Court of Appeal.
As a result of the accident, none of the detainees were injured.
In order to transfer them to the other van, the guards surrounded the back of the cars, and the detainees came out at speed, two by two.
"The incident has not been reported to the police, because the drivers of the two vehicles have agreed amicably regarding the damages that need to be to be paid," Chief Commissioner Madalin Ţăranu said.
The Great Migrations
Romania isn’t and won't be prepared for what's to come.
What about Europe?
I say it from the very beginning, clearly and clearly: the 7000 refugees that Romania should and must naturalize represent, in itself, an insignificant number, but huge compared to the capacity of the Romanian state to manage such a project.
For Romania, even the voluntary quota proposed by Bucharest, in the amount of about 1500 souls, goes far beyond the good intentions of solidarity with the European Union expressed in recent months.
Certainly, if those migrants actually agree to settle in our localities, the chances of integrating them quickly into the Romanian society are extraordinarily small.
I'm convinced they'll be the first to lose their patience.
Parasied by interlopers and crippled by a venal political class, the Romanian state proves impotent in all areas.
Unsuccess to integrate Gypsies is a trivial example.
On top of this, governments of any color have not been able to abduct European funds, to make modern roads, kindergartens or schools, to ensure decent medical assistance, to raise the miserie on the street, to create honorable paid jobs or to keep their own young generation at home.
Why would the refugees settle in another country they are fleeing from?
But what produces much wonder is in particular the hypocrisy with which such a crisis is treated.
We first encounter the beliccious hypocrisiness of strong EU states, which show maximum generosity when it comes to dividing tribulations with the smaller countries.
Then comes the fearful hypocrisiness of the Romanians who, although they have millions of relatives scattered all over the world, do not yet accept the other - of a different language, of a different religion, of a different blood.
Probably for the fear of stealing the national being.
After all, there is also a hypocrisy of many migrants, who, while invocating only the horrors of war as a reason for leaving, do not accept an exodus destination other than Germany or the Nordic countries.
However, not all the refugees are Syrians, and there is no war in Pakistan.
Also, the simplistic way in which the crisis is being analysed can only be mocked.
The causes must be abolished, some argue and, relying strictly on the book of Political Correctivity, they call for peace and investment for migrant countries of origin.
But there's peace in Romania, and from time to time, some foreign capital in the national economy comes from time to time - but that doesn't prevent tens of thousands of Romanians from leaving their country every year.
- Why is he leaving?
In this crisis, the European Union revealed itself to us as an ankylosed, dismantled and obsolicited construction.
I was decrying the fact that Romania is not capable of inventing a country-by-country project either.
Imprompts and Threats Don't Help.
Then, what is the use of the EU, if the only advantage enjoyed by Romanians - the right to free movement could be questioned because of the waves of refugees who cross the borders as if through the cheese?
At some point, the war in Syria will come to an end.
But it's not the migrant crisis.
In the coming decades, overcrowsion, poverty, climate change, resource depletion, etc. will push millions of desperate migrants, from Asia and especially from Africa, towards a better life.
With such politicians, Romania is not and will never be ready for what is to come.
7,000 euros a year to rent the Pogor Club.
Destination practically imposed
Auction for the concessionation concerns a period of 10 years.
According to 7 years in which it remained closed, the club in the courtyard of the Romanian Literature Museum is offered by the County Council for a concession for a period of 10 years.
