Luca defends Silviu Ovidiu Burada, who received the highest punishment in this case.
How Judges Motivated Their Sentence
At the end of the last week, the magistrate of the Vaslui Judgment who convicted the seven young people motivated the sentencing.
In the reasoning, the judge talks about the defiant reaction of the defendants, but also those who supported them, specifying that such attitudes create a strong sense of indignation among the public opinion.
"The court notes that after placing under the pre-emptive measure of judicial control, a restrictive measure of freedom but not deprivation of demigration, under the implied attitude of the indictees, their local families and supporters, a strong sense of indignation was felt at the level of the local and national community regarding the fact that persons accused of serious acts are tried under a less restrictive measure," reads the reasoning of the Vaslui Court.
The magistrates also dismantled the main defense of the seven indictees who during the trial invoked the fact that the girl they violated would not be "church door".
"The court underlines that it is irrelevant the moral quality of the injured person, an woman that the defendants wished to point out through the defenses they have formulated, because the physical and sexual freedom of a person cannot be violated under any provocation," it said.
