Constantin Brâncuși was born on February 19, 1876, in Hobița, a small village in Peeștișani, Gorj County, at the foot of the Carpathians.
He's the Fifth Child of Maria and Radu Nicolae Brâncuși.
Although he came from a wealthy peasant family, Brâncuşi leads a modest life, but one from which he would gather the landmarks that will guide his late artistic vision.
Reminiscent of his childhood and the places where he grew up, the artist confessed, in a meeting with Petre Ţuţea, in Paris, in 1933: "At that time life was beautiful and harmonious".
Millennines, people were happily leading a patriarchal life.
